,"num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"JPw6YLjtE","title":"Using Server-Sent Events (SSE) to Stream Data in Rails","url":"https://pragmaticpineapple.com/using-server-sent-events-to-stream-data-in-rails/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/using-server-sent-events-sse-to-stream-data-in-rails-jpw6yljte","summary":"Using Server-Sent Events (SSE) to Stream Data in Rails, we show how to use server-sent events to stream data from the server to the client. SSE is designed for a unidirectional data flow. There is no communication from the client to the server other than the initial request.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4794bf2a1877ee3efd2048247d2c272e?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":4,"created_at":"2023-07-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"0TINFSTOw","title":"Control Your Dev Processes with Overmind","url":"https://pragmaticpineapple.com/control-your-dev-processes-with-overmind/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/control-your-dev-processes-with-overmind-0tinfstow","summary":"Control Your Dev Processes with Overmind is a tool written by DarthSim and you can view its code at this GitHub repo. Overmind uses a terminal multiplexer under the hood to bring out some useful features. The connect feature is very powerful because it allows you to see the logs of all processes split into tabs.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6fb5d8c1c93c790afe11e7f0590fec83?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2023-07-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"L9aSx5O4j","title":"How to Upload Files in Angular","url":"https://pragmaticpineapple.com/how-to-upload-files-in-angular/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-upload-files-in-angular-l9asx5o4j","summary":"How to Upload Files in Angular | Pragmatic Pineapple. How to upload files in Angular is a simple application with a user-friendly interface to upload single and multiple files. We'll also figure out how to streamline the development workflow using the Uploadcare widget and implement file-uploading functionality in just a few minutes.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/36381fcd2badbd6e0a945cf85d45d27a?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"EfQWzVZRR","title":"How to Upload File in React","url":"https://pragmaticpineapple.com/how-to-upload-file-in-react/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-upload-file-in-react-efqwzvzrr","summary":"How to Upload File in React will show you exactly how to upload a single file in React with fetch. The majority of the code will stay the code from the previous section.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ab5b5de821a15bb2bc4858e00fa1ef78?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":21,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-06-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"Gyi9cEZGD","title":"A Guide to Handling Errors in Preact","url":"https://pragmaticpineapple.com/a-guide-to-handling-errors-in-preact/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-guide-to-handling-errors-in-preact-gyi9cezgd","summary":"Catching Rendering Errors in Preact is a lightweight React alternative, similar rules to the React world also apply here. You can\u2019t use the classic method of resolving errors while rendering because it\u2019s meant to handle imperative code. To properly handle rendering errors, you can use two approaches: hook and hook.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7c1d71c657d76c9802433f76bcdaccd8?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-05-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"cUTEMW17x","title":"How to Sync Your Storybook Design System Into Figma","url":"https://pragmaticpineapple.com/how-to-sync-your-storybook-design-system-into-figma/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-sync-your-storybook-design-system-into-figma-cutemw17x","su